uld have [rival]'s best teacher."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"Gain a Scribe"},{"text":"+30–300 Culture (by city tier)","yield":"culture"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["aeAddSpecialistClasses: SPECIALISTCLASS_SCRIBE","aeBonuses: BONUS_CULTURE_GAIN_AVERAGE"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_THE_MAXIMS_OF_PTAHHOTEP_OPTION_1_CITY","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Provide him with a position where he may continue writing."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"Begin project: Archive I"},{"base":60,"per":15,"text":"+60 Civics (+15/city)","yield":"civics"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["aeAddProjects: PROJECT_ARCHIVE_1","aeBonuses: BONUS_CIVICS_GAIN_AVERAGE"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_THE_MAXIMS_OF_PTAHHOTEP_OPTION_2_CITY","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Fund a school teaching The Maxims of Ptahhotep."}],"prob":25,"subjects":["City Us","Tutor Egypt Ptahhotep","Player Us","Leader Us"],"text":"Leaders of [city] sing the praises of the lowly city administrator who has revolutionized their local government. His name is Ptahhotep, and he has expressed great interest in serving the king's royal court. According to those who know him, Ptahhotep is especially skilled with mentorship and education. His writings on courtly conduct are used by teachers across [rival].","timing":{"repeat":"Once per game"},"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptahhotep","weight":1},{"author":"Leyla Johnson","conditions":["City Discontent Moderate","Player Max Three Courtiers"],"id":"EVENTSTORY_RAMPANT_CORRUPTION","name":"Rampant Corruption","options":[{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"+1 Happiness level"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["iHappinessLevels 1"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_RAMPANT_CORRUPTION_ALLOW","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Allow the campaign to proceed unhindered."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"+2 Happiness levels"},{"base":-320,"per":-80,"text":"-320 Money (-80/city)","yield":"money"}]}